{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q45VUQTBaPSarU8beiutiW","type":"tool_result","content":"126	- `FND-0168` [corroborated; {'ambient': 'smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack Mbar_{6,6} of dimension 21 with boundary D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6}, D proper', 'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['that K fails to be Tate of type Q(-8)', 'that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate', 'that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K', 'any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) or of the RED-0001 target', 'any claim outside (g,n)=(6,6), although the logical structure of clauses (2)-(4) is general', 'any refutation of ATT-0116 clause (a) or of CL-01 through CL-04, which the audit confirms'], 'hypotheses': ['M_{6,6} smooth, so H^k_c(M_{6,6};Q) has weights <= k', 'D proper, so H^{15}(D;Q) has weights <= 15', 'morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict, so Gr^W_k is exact', 'Q-coefficients throughout; stack-level Betti cohomology, no integral or coarse-space content', "for clause (3), a closed support in M_{6,6} must be fixed before the phrase 'contribution supported on Z' has a referent"], 'objects': ['K = ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q))', 'Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q)', 'RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', 'balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus Z and any closure of its image in M_{6,6}', 'ATT-0116 theorem clause (b) and claim CL-05'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Scope: (g,n)=(6,6) over C with Q-coefficients; Mbar_{6,6} the smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension d=21, D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6} its proper boundary, Z the balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus. (1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6} -- and is canonically the Hodge-structure dual of the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), with Q(-8) dual to Q(8). This uses only smoothness of M_{6,6} (weights of H^{16}_c are <= 16), properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15) and strictness. It is a global invariant of M_{6,6} and carries no support condition. The separate Poincare identification W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21) (FND-0001) is a different map and must not be conflated with this duality. (2) For any pure Q-Hodge structure V of weight 16, 'V is a finite direct sum of Q(-8)' and 'V is spanned by its Hodge (8,8)-classes' are the same condition (V_C = V^{8,8}) by the definition of Hodge type; neither polarizability nor semisimplicity of the category of pure polarizable weight-16 Q-Hodge structures is needed for this equivalence, and neither adds information to it. Applied to K, the equivalence is a restatement of the target, not a reduction: it imposes no support condition and produces no cycle class. (Semisimplicity, per FND-0033, only excludes extension gaps at this corner.) (3) Give 'the contribution supported on Z' its only standard meaning by first fixing a closed support Y in M_{6,6} containing the image of Z. Since Gr^W is exact on mixed Hodge structures, the Borel-Moore localization sequence yields an exact sequence W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q). Consequently: (3a) if the Z-supported contribution means the image of the first map, then K Tate of type Q(-8) implies that contribution is Tate (a sub-object of a type-(8,8) structure is of type (8,8)), so Z-Tate is necessary; but the converse -- the direction the reduction needs -- does not follow, since it additionally requires a support-exhaustion input, namely vanishing or Tate-ness of the quotient injecting into W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} of the complement of Y. No such input is established for (6,6). (3b) if it means W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself, then neither direction follows, since only the image of that group is constrained by K. ATT-0116 fixes neither reading. Hence the asserted equivalence 'the contribution supported on Z is Tate of the exact target type if and only if K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes' is unproved and is a non-sequitur in its load-bearing direction. This is a statement about a missing hypothesis, not a demonstration that the two sides have different truth values: if the RED-0001 target is Tate, both sides hold, so the biconditional cannot be refuted by exhibiting differing truth values. (4) 'K is spanned by algebraic fundamental classes of codimension-8 cycles of Mbar_{6,6} supported on a closure of Z' implies 'K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes', but the converse is the Hodge conjecture in codimension 8 on the 21-dimensional Mbar_{6,6}, which is unproved in general beyond the (1,1) case; writing 'equivalently' between the two silently assumes it. (5) Independently of (3) and (4), the support clause carries two further undischarged obligations: (5a) a closed (stratified) embedding of the balanced reduced-support model into M_{6,6}/Mbar_{6,6} together with a Gysin map -- that model is an open piece of the failure locus (FND-0052), and FND-0147 supplies only a representable unramified quasi-finite monomorphism to M_{6,6}, which is not a closed immersion of a pure-codimension-4 closed substack; (5b) the Gysin degree shift H^{8}(Z-tilde;Q)(-4) -> H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) for a 17-dimensional codimension-4 support with a suitable smooth model Z-tilde. The phrase 'codimension-8 cycles supported on the closure of Z' is itself degree-consistent (codimension 8 in Mbar_{6,6} equals codimension 4 on the 17-dimensional support), so the defect is the unwritten shift and the missing closed embedding, not the codimension label; the fundamental class of the support itself lies in H^{8}, not H^{16}. Not asserted: that K fails to be Tate; that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate; that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K; any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q); any claim for (g,n) other than (6,6), although the logical structure of (2)-(4) is general. Confirmed and untouched: ATT-0116 clause (a) and claims CL-01 through CL-04.
127	- `FND-0169` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'the global kernel K', 'RED-0001', 'nonconstant coefficient objects'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'j': 8, 'objects': ['reduced separated finite-type C-scheme bases carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16', 'hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167']}]: Over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] be the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15 of balanced genus-six degree-four covers (FND-0162). Let S range over reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family in the sense of FND-0167, including connected components of reduced separated finite-type etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal. The constant-coefficient corner Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) is not an invariant of the stack Hbar^bal: it depends on S. Explicitly, the mu_3-Kummer cover C->M_{0,4} cut out by y^3=x(x-1), with smooth projective model Cbar of genus one, yields a nonempty irreducible finite-etale cover Mtilde of M_{0,18} whose Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Mtilde;Q) contains a nonzero Hodge type (15,1), obtained as the compact-support Kunneth summand Q(-1) tensor H^{1,0}(Cbar)^{tensor 14} and surviving removal of the pairwise-diagonal locus of dimension at most 14 because Hodge numbers of compactly supported cohomology vanish in filtration degree strictly larger than dimension (Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)). By the Bujokas-Patel theorem that the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle F of a general cover in the classical simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g} is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (hence for (d,g)=(4,6)), together with FND-0159 (the classical Hurwitz space is etale over the configuration space of r=2g+2d-2=18 points), there is a connected finite-etale Hurwitz chart X over M_{0,18} whose balanced open is nonempty. Finite-etale pullback/trace of the type-(15,1) class along a connected component Xtilde of X times_{M_{0,18}} Mtilde, followed by compact-support localization onto the balanced open V of Xtilde (FND-0165), produces a connected smooth 15-fold V, etale over Hbar^bal, with Gr^{15,1} Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;C) nonzero. Thus Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8). For any allowed atlas U, the disjoint union U sqcup V is again an allowed atlas and compactly supported cohomology is additive, so the same non-Tate summand appears in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U sqcup V;Q). Consequently the j=8 instance of hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167, namely that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8), is false for some allowed S. FND-0167 itself does not assert (H-S). Any campaign statement that asserts or requires (H-S) while universally quantifying over a reduced locally Noetherian scheme atlas of Hbar^bal, or over all reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying the balanced setup, is therefore false as stated rather than merely unproved. (H-S) may be asserted only for a specifically named atlas, or replaced by a stack-level statement, which requires a compact-support mixed-Hodge formalism for Deligne-Mumford stacks that FND-0165 explicitly withholds. This does not address Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U): the FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into a sum of Tate twists of corners of S, so it cannot transport non-Tateness from S to Z, and the discriminant in the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle has dimension 16 so F^{15} H_c^{16} need not vanish there.
128	- `FND-0170` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimension': 'd>=2', 'excludes': ['merely dominant morphisms that are neither finite etale nor open immersions', 'compactly supported mixed Hodge theory of Deligne-Mumford stacks without a scheme atlas', 'non-Tateness of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for the Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model', 'RED-0001'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'includes': 'every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3', 'objects': ['smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold W', 'finite etale morphism W->M_{0,d+3} or dense open immersion W->M_{0,d+3}', "connected component W' of the base change of the product mu_3-Kummer cover"], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let d≥2 be an integer. Let B=M_{0,4}≅P^1 minus {0,1,∞}. Let Cbar be the smooth projective connected curve with function field C(x,y) and equation y^3=x(x-1): the degree-three map Cbar→P^1 given by x is totally ramified over exactly 0,1,∞ (valuations of x(x-1) equal 1,1,−2, none divisible by 3), and Riemann-Hurwitz gives 2g(Cbar)−2=3(−2)+3(2)=0, so Cbar has genus one. Let C be Cbar minus those three ramification points, so C→B is connected finite etale of degree three. Compact-support localization yields Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q)≅H^1(Cbar;Q) of Hodge types (1,0) and (0,1), and H_c^2(C;Q)≅Q(−1); also H_c^0(C)=0. Identifying M_{0,d+3} with the complement of the pairwise diagonals in B^d, set Mtilde:=C^d ×_{B^d} M_{0,d+3}. This is a nonempty Zariski-open in the irreducible d-fold C^d, hence irreducible, and Mtilde→M_{0,d+3} is connected finite etale. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places, for each of the d choices of factor, a direct summand Q(−1)⊗(Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{⊗(d−1)} inside Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(C^d;Q); the Hodge component (1,1)+(d−1)·(1,0)=(d,1) is one-dimensional and nonzero. The inverse image Y of the pairwise diagonals has dimension ≤d−1, so the Hodge numbers of H_c^{d+1}(Y) vanish for p>dim Y and therefore F^d H_c^{d+1}(Y;C)=0. Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for W and F; weights of H_c^d(Y;Q) are at most d; hence Gr^W_{d+1} of the compact-support localization sequence H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde)→H_c^{d+1}(C^d)→H_c^{d+1}(Y) is exact (FND-0165), the type-(d,1) class dies in H_c^{d+1}(Y), and it lifts to a nonzero class of Hodge type (d,1) in Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;Q). In particular F^d Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;C)≠0. For d≥2 one has d>(d+1)/2, so this weight-equals-degree corner is non-Tate. Now let W be a smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold equipped with a finite etale morphism f:W→M_{0,d+3}, and let W' be any connected component of W×_{M_{0,d+3}} Mtilde. Then W'→W is finite etale of positive degree, W'→Mtilde is finite etale of positive degree, and finite-etale pullback/trace over Q injects the type-(d,1) class into Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(W';Q). The same non-Tate class is obtained if instead f is a dense open immersion, by a second application of FND-0165 to the complement of dimension ≤d−1. Consequently the property that Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(−;Q) is Tate is not invariant under finite etale refinement of any such base, and no Tate assertion for that corner can be proved by an argument that is invariant under finite etale pullback, transfer, averaging, monodromy-orbit counting, or descent along an etale scheme atlas. This applies in particular to every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3. The statement does not apply to a merely dominant morphism that is neither finite etale nor an open immersion; it does not assert anything about compactly supported cohomology of a Deligne-Mumford stack in the absence of a scheme atlas; and it does not transport non-Tateness to Gr^W_{16} H_c^{16}(Z;Q) of a Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model, nor to RED-0001.
129	- `FND-0171` [corroborated; {'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimensions': {'A': 17, 'Delta': 16, 'S': 15}, 'g': 6, 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['S a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying (CE)+(N)+(BAL)', 'L fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, formation of pi_*L commuting with base change, so A=P_S(pi_*L) is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle', 'U=A minus Delta is the reduced-support open', 'Z=Ord(U)->U is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings'], 'n': 6, 'objects': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}', 'T_16(Z)'], 'setup': 'FND-0167 balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model Z=Ord(U)'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients in the FND-0167 setup for (g,n)=(6,6). Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family whose relative degree-six line bundle L is fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, so that formation of pi_*L commutes with base change. Put A=P_S(pi_*L), a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle of dimension 17; let Delta be the non-reduced-divisor locus; put U=A minus Delta; and let Z=Ord(U)->U be the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. FND-0167 supplies an injection of pure polarizable weight-16 Hodge structures Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^12(S;Q)(-2), obtained by composing the FND-0165 corner injection for the open immersion U subset A with the projective-bundle formula for A->S. Polarizable pure Q-Hodge structures of a fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category, so this injection propagates Tate type of Q(-8) from the three constant-coefficient S-corners (H-S) down to U and to the S_6-invariants of T_16(Z). It cannot propagate non-Tate type from S to U or to Z: a non-Tate ambient Hodge structure may contain a Tate subobject, and FND-0167 does not assert surjectivity of the corner map. Independently, fibrewise Bertini (the general member of |L| consists of six distinct points) together with the classical discriminant and dual-curve description of a spanned g^2_6 in |L| isomorphic to P^2 imply that Delta->S is nonempty of pure relative dimension one, hence dim Delta=16. Deligne's Hodge-number bound (h^{p,q}=0 for p greater than the dimension) therefore does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0, so the type-(15,1) lifting argument used by ATT-0118, which requires the removed locus to have dimension at most 14, does not lift classes from A to U. Consequently ATT-0118's refutation of (H-S) at j=8 on an allowed atlas component does not refute Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) or Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), both of which remain open. A repair of C66-TATE-SUPPORT that treats the Z-clause as refuted by base-corner non-Tateness is invalid. The universally quantified base and universal-curve conjunct should be dropped or replaced by a named-atlas hypothesis; even on a named atlas, FND-0167 controls only Z^{S_6} via (H-S) and the [6] and [5,1] multiplicity spaces via (H-C), not the remaining S_6-isotypics.
130	- `FND-0172` [corroborated; {'applies_to': 'any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover, including any Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'cover': {'F': 'O(4)+O(5)', 'degree': 4, 'genus': 6}, 'does_not_assert': ['Tate-ness of Z=Ord(U) or of RED-0001', 'irreducibility or the number of connected components of H^bal', 'closedness of the composed or type-(ii) locus', 'that CLM-0112-4 is the unique existence route'], 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'objects': ['H=H_{4,6}(P^1)', 'H^bal', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'simply-branched locus', 'classical Hurwitz space H_{4,6}']}]: Let k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let H=H_{4,6}(P^1) be the Deligne-Mumford stack of finite degree-four covers of a fixed P^1 by smooth connected genus-six curves, and let H^bal be the open locus where the Casnati-Ekedahl relations bundle in the packet orientation F=ker(Sym^2 E -> gamma_*(omega_{C/P^1}^{otimes 2})) is isomorphic to O_{P^1}(4)+O_{P^1}(5) (rank two, degree +9). Write Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]. Call gamma simply branched when every geometric fibre has partition type 2+1+1+1, equivalently when every local monodromy permutation in S_4 is a transposition, equivalently when gamma has eighteen distinct simple branch values. (1) The packet's self-contained nonemptiness witness for H^bal (FND-0154: gamma=q o psi through a smooth genus-one curve) is never simply branched. This is FND-0158: a nontrivial factorization C->Y->P^1 of degrees (2,2) has a fibre of type (2,2) or 4 over each branch value of q, since every degree-two map Y->P^1 is ramified (Riemann-Hurwitz: deg R_q=2g_Y+2>=2); equivalently, a simply-branched connected degree-four cover has monodromy group S_4, which is primitive, while a nontrivial factorization is imprimitive. Under the extra reducedness and disjointness hypotheses of FND-0158(b), the FND-0154 family has fourteen branch values (ten of type 2+1+1 and four of type (2,2)), and the set of simply-branched type-(ii) points is empty. Consequently FND-0154 may not be cited as a simply-branched balanced cover. (2) Existence of a simply-branched point of H^bal, equivalently of Hbar^bal, is not supplied by FND-0154, nor by the type-(i) density statement of FND-0162 (type (i) means not FND-0153 type (ii), which excludes only the bielliptic-through-a-plane-cubic case and still permits primitive non-simple ramification). Any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover — in particular any argument that places a Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18 inside the balanced locus — must discharge existence by one of the following routes. Route A (packet-internal dimension comparison): H is smooth of pure dimension 18 at every point, independently of ramification profile (FND-0159). The classical Hurwitz space of a fixed ramification profile with r distinct branch values is etale over the configuration space of those r points and has dimension r, which equals 18 if and only if the cover is simply branched (FND-0159; Kanev, arXiv:math/0509154, Introduction: the discriminant map of the simply-branched Hurwitz space is etale onto Y^{(n)}-Delta, with Delta the codimension-one locus of non-simple divisors). Hence the non-simply-branched locus in H has dimension at most 17. Combined with nonemptiness of H^bal (FND-0154) and the fact that H^bal is open of pure dimension 18 (FND-0162, FND-0163), every nonempty connected component of H^bal, and of the quotient Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15, meets the simply-branched locus. Equivalently, after the PGL_2 quotient, the same comparison is the dual-confirmed bound dim(non-simply-branched)<=14 in Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15 recorded as CLM-0112-4. Route B (Bujokas-Patel genericity): for a general point of the classical irreducible simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g}, the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of quadrics F is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (Bujokas-Patel, arXiv:1504.03756v1, IMRN 2021, Main Theorem; algebraically closed field of characteristic zero). Here F is defined by 0->F->Sym^2 E->alpha_*(omega_alpha^{otimes 2})->0, with rk F=d(d-3)/2 and deg F=(d-3)(g+d-1), and balanced means h^1(End F)=0. At (d,g)=(4,6) one has g=6>=3, rk F=2, deg F=9, hence F isomorphic to O(4)+O(5), matching the packet orientation. This route does not use FND-0154. FND-0163 records it only inside a NOT ASSERTED clause, so a proof that invokes it must cite the theorem independently. (3) This existence hinge is inherited by every argument that realises an etale chart of Hbar^bal over M_{0,18} or Conf_18. It does not by itself control Gr^W_16 H_c^{16} of the evaluation-failure model Z, nor the campaign target RED-0001.
