arison is internal to that kernel-form family and does not constrain other constructions of subobjects of T. Two consequences: (i) the obligation that no class in T supported on a closed subset contained in the image of Z, or in its closure, be omitted is one-sided (the kernel may contain classes supported on extra components of Y, including points of the Zariski closure of Im that do not lie in Im) and is already met by every such Y, in particular by Y_0; (ii) a strictly larger kernel-form term cannot be obtained from a closed support contained in Y_0, so enlarging the kernel-form term toward exhaustion T_{Z,Y}=T requires a closed support not contained in Y_0 and therefore not equal to the reduced CE classifying-image closure. That extra support is not identified with the CE geometry by the kernel-form interface and is not shown Tate by that construction; showing any enlarged term Tate remains a separate C66-TATE-SUPPORT obligation. Support-exhaustion T_{Z,Y}=T is not asserted for any Y, and vanishing of restriction from T to a nonempty complement is not asserted.
137	- `FND-0184` [corroborated; {'campaign_objects': ['H^bal', 'M_{6,6}', 'PGL_2', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'ATT-0112/CLM-0112-7', 'ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8'], 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': None, 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero, or C', 'hypotheses': ['H and X are algebraic stacks', 'atlases are smooth and surjective of finite type, with source an algebraic space (or a scheme)', 'the classifying morphism is functorial in the 2-Yoneda sense, so tautological families pull back along morphisms of atlases', 'a morphism [H/G]->X, or equality of geometric images from H and from [H/G], requires a separate G-equivariance/G-invariance hypothesis'], 'not_covered': ['transfer of the ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8 scheme-level P^2-bundle/ordering-torsor model from atlases of H^bal to etale atlases of [H^bal/PGL_2]', 'atlas-independence of compactly supported cohomology of the atlas', 'constructibility of S (Chevalley), which is used in CLM-0120-2 but is not required for independence of the reduced closure', 'Tate type, Gysin maps, closed embeddings of Z, or support-exhaustion'], 'objects': ['algebraic stacks H and X', 'smooth surjective finite-type atlases from algebraic spaces', "2-fibre product W=V x_H V'", 'classifying morphisms f_V:Z_V->X', 'geometric image S in |X|', 'reduced closed substack Y', 'quotient presentation [H/G]']}]: Let H and X be algebraic stacks. Suppose a subset S of the geometric points |X| is defined as the image of a classifying morphism attached functorially, in the 2-Yoneda sense, to smooth surjective finite-type atlases of H: for every such atlas V->H from an algebraic space there is a finite-type morphism f_V:Z_V->X, and these morphisms are compatible with pullback along morphisms of atlases. Then for any two such atlases V->H and V'->H, the 2-fibre product W=V x_H V' exists as an algebraic space (Stacks Project Tag 04T2); the projections W->V and W->V' are smooth and surjective, hence surjective on geometric points (Tags 04XH, 04XI); and W->H is again a smooth surjective atlas. If Z_(-) is constructed only for scheme bases, one must pass to a scheme presentation of W. The tautological family on Z_W is then the pullback of the families on Z_V and Z_{V'}, so the geometric images of f_V, f_{V'}, and f_W in |X| coincide. Consequently S is independent of the atlas, and the unique reduced closed substack Y of X with |Y| equal to the Zariski closure of S (Tag 0509) is independent of the atlas. Common refinement of atlases of H does not by itself produce a morphism [H/G]->X or identify S with the image arising from an atlas of the quotient: a morphism [H/G]->X exists if and only if the classifying morphism from H is G-equivariant, equivalently the X-valued moduli point is G-invariant on geometric points (Tag 04WM). This lemma does not assert that a scheme-level tautological model constructed on atlases of H transfers to etale atlases of [H/G], and it does not assert atlas-independence of compactly supported cohomology of the atlas. In the campaign case (g,n)=(6,6), with H=H^bal the balanced tetragonal stack, X=M_{6,6}, and G=PGL_2, the extra invariance is ATT-0112/CLM-0112-7; the failure of ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8 to transfer to atlases of Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] is the separate finding FND-0187."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d394240-b9f5-488a-8bd9-c3fe5dc1a28f","uuid":"c64de8e5-09f5-4499-9086-5cae778b9a97","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:44:21.387Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/r_/40tyr0nj6zn_yqb74rw_351c0000gn/T/pure-tate-agent-rp38w_bp/proof/packets/generated/C66BAR-001-v2.md","content":"- `FND-0168` [corroborated; {'ambient': 'smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack Mbar_{6,6} of dimension 21 with boundary D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6}, D proper', 'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['that K fails to be Tate of type Q(-8)', 'that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate', 'that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K', 'any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) or of the RED-0001 target', 'any claim outside (g,n)=(6,6), although the logical structure of clauses (2)-(4) is general', 'any refutation of ATT-0116 clause (a) or of CL-01 through CL-04, which the audit confirms'], 'hypotheses': ['M_{6,6} smooth, so H^k_c(M_{6,6};Q) has weights <= k', 'D proper, so H^{15}(D;Q) has weights <= 15', 'morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict, so Gr^W_k is exact', 'Q-coefficients throughout; stack-level Betti cohomology, no integral or coarse-space content', "for clause (3), a closed support in M_{6,6} must be fixed before the phrase 'contribution supported on Z' has a referent"], 'objects': ['K = ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q))', 'Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q)', 'RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', 'balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus Z and any closure of its image in M_{6,6}', 'ATT-0116 theorem clause (b) and claim CL-05'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Scope: (g,n)=(6,6) over C with Q-coefficients; Mbar_{6,6} the smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension d=21, D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6} its proper boundary, Z the balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus. (1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6} -- and is canonically the Hodge-structure dual of the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), with Q(-8) dual to Q(8). This uses only smoothness of M_{6,6} (weights of H^{16}_c are <= 16), properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15) and strictness. It is a global invariant of M_{6,6} and carries no support condition. The separate Poincare identification W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21) (FND-0001) is a different map and must not be conflated with this duality. (2) For any pure Q-Hodge structure V of weight 16, 'V is a finite direct sum of Q(-8)' and 'V is spanned by its Hodge (8,8)-classes' are the same condition (V_C = V^{8,8}) by the definition of Hodge type; neither polarizability nor semisimplicity of the category of pure polarizable weight-16 Q-Hodge structures is needed for this equivalence, and neither adds information to it. Applied to K, the equivalence is a restatement of the target, not a reduction: it imposes no support condition and produces no cycle class. (Semisimplicity, per FND-0033, only excludes extension gaps at this corner.) (3) Give 'the contribution supported on Z' its only standard meaning by first fixing a closed support Y in M_{6,6} containing the image of Z. Since Gr^W is exact on mixed Hodge structures, the Borel-Moore localization sequence yields an exact sequence W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q). Consequently: (3a) if the Z-supported contribution means the image of the first map, then K Tate of type Q(-8) implies that contribution is Tate (a sub-object of a type-(8,8) structure is of type (8,8)), so Z-Tate is necessary; but the converse -- the direction the reduction needs -- does not follow, since it additionally requires a support-exhaustion input, namely vanishing or Tate-ness of the quotient injecting into W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} of the complement of Y. No such input is established for (6,6). (3b) if it means W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself, then neither direction follows, since only the image of that group is constrained by K. ATT-0116 fixes neither reading. Hence the asserted equivalence 'the contribution supported on Z is Tate of the exact target type if and only if K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes' is unproved and is a non-sequitur in its load-bearing direction. This is a statement about a missing hypothesis, not a demonstration that the two sides have different truth values: if the RED-0001 target is Tate, both sides hold, so the biconditional cannot be refuted by exhibiting differing truth values. (4) 'K is spanned by algebraic fundamental classes of codimension-8 cycles of Mbar_{6,6} supported on a closure of Z' implies 'K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes', but the converse is the Hodge conjecture in codimension 8 on the 21-dimensional Mbar_{6,6}, which is unproved in general beyond the (1,1) case; writing 'equivalently' between the two silently assumes it. (5) Independently of (3) and (4), the support clause carries two further undischarged obligations: (5a) a closed (stratified) embedding of the balanced reduced-support model into M_{6,6}/Mbar_{6,6} together with a Gysin map -- that model is an open piece of the failure locus (FND-0052), and FND-0147 supplies only a representable unramified quasi-finite monomorphism to M_{6,6}, which is not a closed immersion of a pure-codimension-4 closed substack; (5b) the Gysin degree shift H^{8}(Z-tilde;Q)(-4) -> H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) for a 17-dimensional codimension-4 support with a suitable smooth model Z-tilde. The phrase 'codimension-8 cycles supported on the closure of Z' is itself degree-consistent (codimension 8 in Mbar_{6,6} equals codimension 4 on the 17-dimensional support), so the defect is the unwritten shift and the missing closed embedding, not the codimension label; the fundamental class of the support itself lies in H^{8}, not H^{16}. Not asserted: that K fails to be Tate; that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate; that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K; any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q); any claim for (g,n) other than (6,6), although the logical structure of (2)-(4) is general. Confirmed and untouched: ATT-0116 clause (a) and claims CL-01 through CL-04.
- `FND-0169` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'the global kernel K', 'RED-0001', 'nonconstant coefficient objects'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'j': 8, 'objects': ['reduced separated finite-type C-scheme bases carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16', 'hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167']}]: Over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] be the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15 of balanced genus-six degree-four covers (FND-0162). Let S range over reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family in the sense of FND-0167, including connected components of reduced separated finite-type etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal. The constant-coefficient corner Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) is not an invariant of the stack Hbar^bal: it depends on S. Explicitly, the mu_3-Kummer cover C->M_{0,4} cut out by y^3=x(x-1), with smooth projective model Cbar of genus one, yields a nonempty irreducible finite-etale cover Mtilde of M_{0,18} whose Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Mtilde;Q) contains a nonzero Hodge type (15,1), obtained as the compact-support Kunneth summand Q(-1) tensor H^{1,0}(Cbar)^{tensor 14} and surviving removal of the pairwise-diagonal locus of dimension at most 14 because Hodge numbers of compactly supported cohomology vanish in filtration degree strictly larger than dimension (Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)). By the Bujokas-Patel theorem that the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle F of a general cover in the classical simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g} is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (hence for (d,g)=(4,6)), together with FND-0159 (the classical Hurwitz space is etale over the configuration space of r=2g+2d-2=18 points), there is a connected finite-etale Hurwitz chart X over M_{0,18} whose balanced open is nonempty. Finite-etale pullback/trace of the type-(15,1) class along a connected component Xtilde of X times_{M_{0,18}} Mtilde, followed by compact-support localization onto the balanced open V of Xtilde (FND-0165), produces a connected smooth 15-fold V, etale over Hbar^bal, with Gr^{15,1} Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;C) nonzero. Thus Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8). For any allowed atlas U, the disjoint union U sqcup V is again an allowed atlas and compactly supported cohomology is additive, so the same non-Tate summand appears in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U sqcup V;Q). Consequently the j=8 instance of hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167, namely that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8), is false for some allowed S. FND-0167 itself does not assert (H-S). Any campaign statement that asserts or requires (H-S) while universally quantifying over a reduced locally Noetherian scheme atlas of Hbar^bal, or over all reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying the balanced setup, is therefore false as stated rather than merely unproved. (H-S) may be asserted only for a specifically named atlas, or replaced by a stack-level statement, which requires a compact-support mixed-Hodge formalism for Deligne-Mumford stacks that FND-0165 explicitly withholds. This does not address Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U): the FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into a sum of Tate twists of corners of S, so it cannot transport non-Tateness from S to Z, and the discriminant in the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle has dimension 16 so F^{15} H_c^{16} need not vanish there.
- `FND-0170` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimension': 'd>=2', 'excludes': ['merely dominant morphisms that are neither finite etale nor open immersions', 'compactly supported mixed Hodge theory of Deligne-Mumford stacks without a scheme atlas', 'non-Tateness of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for the Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model', 'RED-0001'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'includes': 'every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3', 'objects': ['smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold W', 'finite etale morphism W->M_{0,d+3} or dense open immersion W->M_{0,d+3}', "connected component W' of the base change of the product mu_3-Kummer cover"], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let d≥2 be an integer. Let B=M_{0,4}≅P^1 minus {0,1,∞}. Let Cbar be the smooth projective connected curve with function field C(x,y) and equation y^3=x(x-1): the degree-three map Cbar→P^1 given by x is totally ramified over exactly 0,1,∞ (valuations of x(x-1) equal 1,1,−2, none divisible by 3), and Riemann-Hurwitz gives 2g(Cbar)−2=3(−2)+3(2)=0, so Cbar has genus one. Let C be Cbar minus those three ramification points, so C→B is connected finite etale of degree three. Compact-support localization yields Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q)≅H^1(Cbar;Q) of Hodge types (1,0) and (0,1), and H_c^2(C;Q)≅Q(−1); also H_c^0(C)=0. Identifying M_{0,d+3} with the complement of the pairwise diagonals in B^d, set Mtilde:=C^d ×_{B^d} M_{0,d+3}. This is a nonempty Zariski-open in the irreducible d-fold C^d, hence irreducible, and Mtilde→M_{0,d+3} is connected finite etale. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places, for each of the d choices of factor, a direct summand Q(−1)⊗(Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{⊗(d−1)} inside Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(C^d;Q); the Hodge component (1,1)+(d−1)·(1,0)=(d,1) is one-dimensional and nonzero. The inverse image Y of the pairwise diagonals has dimension ≤d−1, so the Hodge numbers of H_c^{d+1}(Y) vanish for p>dim Y and therefore F^d H_c^{d+1}(Y;C)=0. Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for W and F; weights of H_c^d(Y;Q) are at most d; hence Gr^W_{d+1} of the compact-support localization sequence H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde)→H_c^{d+1}(C^d)→H_c^{d+1}(Y) is exact (FND-0165), the type-(d,1) class dies in H_c^{d+1}(Y), and it lifts to a nonzero class of Hodge type (d,1) in Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;Q). In particular F^d Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;C)≠0. For d≥2 one has d>(d+1)/2, so this weight-equals-degree corner is non-Tate. Now let W be a smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold equipped with a finite etale morphism f:W→M_{0,d+3}, and let W' be any connected component of W×_{M_{0,d+3}} Mtilde. Then W'→W is finite etale of positive degree, W'→Mtilde is finite etale of positive degree, and finite-etale pullback/trace over Q injects the type-(d,1) class into Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(W';Q). The same non-Tate class is obtained if instead f is a dense open immersion, by a second application of FND-0165 to the complement of dimension ≤d−1. Consequently the property that Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(−;Q) is Tate is not invariant under finite etale refinement of any such base, and no Tate assertion for that corner can be proved by an argument that is invariant under finite etale pullback, transfer, averaging, monodromy-orbit counting, or descent along an etale scheme atlas. This applies in particular to every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3. The statement does not apply to a merely dominant morphism that is neither finite etale nor an open immersion; it does not assert anything about compactly supported cohomology of a Deligne-Mumford stack in the absence of a scheme atlas; and it does not transport non-Tateness to Gr^W_{16} H_c^{16}(Z;Q) of a Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model, nor to RED-0001.
- `FND-0171` [corroborated; {'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimensions': {'A': 17, 'Delta': 16, 'S': 15}, 'g': 6, 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['S a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying (CE)+(N)+(BAL)', 'L fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, formation of pi_*L commuting with base change, so A=P_S(pi_*L) is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle', 'U=A minus Delta is the reduced-support open', 'Z=Ord(U)->U is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings'], 'n': 6, 'objects': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}', 'T_16(Z)'], 'setup': 'FND-0167 balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model Z=Ord(U)'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients in the FND-0167 setup for (g,n)=(6,6). Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family whose relative degree-six line bundle L is fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, so that formation of pi_*L commutes with base change. Put A=P_S(pi_*L), a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle of dimension 17; let Delta be the non-reduced-divisor locus; put U=A minus Delta; and let Z=Ord(U)->U be the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. FND-0167 supplies an injection of pure polarizable weight-16 Hodge structures Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^12(S;Q)(-2), obtained by composing the FND-0165 corner injection for the open immersion U subset A with the projective-bundle formula for A->S. Polarizable pure Q-Hodge structures of a fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category, so this injection propagates Tate type of Q(-8) from the three constant-coefficient S-corners (H-S) down to U and to the S_6-invariants of T_16(Z). It cannot propagate non-Tate type from S to U or to Z: a non-Tate ambient Hodge structure may contain a Tate subobject, and FND-0167 does not assert surjectivity of the corner map. Independently, fibrewise Bertini (the general member of |L| consists of six distinct points) together with the classical discriminant and dual-curve description of a spanned g^2_6 in |L| isomorphic to P^2 imply that Delta->S is nonempty of pure relative dimension one, hence dim Delta=16. Deligne's Hodge-number bound (h^{p,q}=0 for p greater than the dimension) therefore does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0, so the type-(15,1) lifting argument used by ATT-0118, which requires the removed locus to have dimension at most 14, does not lift classes from A to U. Consequently ATT-0118's refutation of (H-S) at j=8 on an allowed atlas component does not refute Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) or Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), both of which remain open. A repair of C66-TATE-SUPPORT that treats the Z-clause as refuted by base-corner non-Tateness is invalid. The universally quantified base and universal-curve conjunct should be dropped or replaced by a named-atlas hypothesis; even on a named atlas, FND-0167 controls only Z^{S_6} via (H-S) and the [6] and [5,1] multiplicity spaces via (H-C), not the remaining S_6-isotypics.
- `FND-0172` [corroborated; {'applies_to': 'any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover, including any Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'cover': {'F': 'O(4)+O(5)', 'degree': 4, 'genus': 6}, 'does_not_assert': ['Tate-ness of Z=Ord(U) or of RED-0001', 'irreducibility or the number of connected components of H^bal', 'closedness of the composed or type-(ii) locus', 'that CLM-0112-4 is the unique existence route'], 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'objects': ['H=H_{4,6}(P^1)', 'H^bal', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'simply-branched locus', 'classical Hurwitz space H_{4,6}']}]: Let k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let H=H_{4,6}(P^1) be the Deligne-Mumford stack of finite degree-four covers of a fixed P^1 by smooth connected genus-six curves, and let H^bal be the open locus where the Casnati-Ekedahl relations bundle in the packet orientation F=ker(Sym^2 E -> gamma_*(omega_{C/P^1}^{otimes 2})) is isomorphic to O_{P^1}(4)+O_{P^1}(5) (rank two, degree +9). Write Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]. Call gamma simply branched when every geometric fibre has partition type 2+1+1+1, equivalently when every local monodromy permutation in S_4 is a transposition, equivalently when gamma has eighteen distinct simple branch values. (1) The packet's self-contained nonemptiness witness for H^bal (FND-0154: gamma=q o psi through a smooth genus-one curve) is never simply branched. This is FND-0158: a nontrivial factorization C->Y->P^1 of degrees (2,2) has a fibre of type (2,2) or 4 over each branch value of q, since every degree-two map Y->P^1 is ramified (Riemann-Hurwitz: deg R_q=2g_Y+2>=2); equivalently, a simply-branched connected degree-four cover has monodromy group S_4, which is primitive, while a nontrivial factorization is imprimitive. Under the extra reducedness and disjointness hypotheses of FND-0158(b), the FND-0154 family has fourteen branch values (ten of type 2+1+1 and four of type (2,2)), and the set of simply-branched type-(ii) points is empty. Consequently FND-0154 may not be cited as a simply-branched balanced cover. (2) Existence of a simply-branched point of H^bal, equivalently of Hbar^bal, is not supplied by FND-0154, nor by the type-(i) density statement of FND-0162 (type (i) means not FND-0153 type (ii), which excludes only the bielliptic-through-a-plane-cubic case and still permits primitive non-simple ramification). Any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover — in particular any argument that places a Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18 inside the balanced locus — must discharge existence by one of the following routes. Route A (packet-internal dimension comparison): H is smooth of pure dimension 18 at every point, independently of ramification profile (FND-0159). The classical Hurwitz space of a fixed ramification profile with r distinct branch values is etale over the configuration space of those r points and has dimension r, which equals 18 if and only if the cover is simply branched (FND-0159; Kanev, arXiv:math/0509154, Introduction: the discriminant map of the simply-branched Hurwitz space is etale onto Y^{(n)}-Delta, with Delta the codimension-one locus of non-simple divisors). Hence the non-simply-branched locus in H has dimension at most 17. Combined with nonemptiness of H^bal (FND-0154) and the fact that H^bal is open of pure dimension 18 (FND-0162, FND-0163), every nonempty connected component of H^bal, and of the quotient Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15, meets the simply-branched locus. Equivalently, after the PGL_2 quotient, the same comparison is the dual-confirmed bound dim(non-simply-branched)<=14 in Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15 recorded as CLM-0112-4. Route B (Bujokas-Patel genericity): for a general point of the classical irreducible simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g}, the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of quadrics F is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (Bujokas-Patel, arXiv:1504.03756v1, IMRN 2021, Main Theorem; algebraically closed field of characteristic zero). Here F is defined by 0->F->Sym^2 E->alpha_*(omega_alpha^{otimes 2})->0, with rk F=d(d-3)/2 and deg F=(d-3)(g+d-1), and balanced means h^1(End F)=0. At (d,g)=(4,6) one has g=6>=3, rk F=2, deg F=9, hence F isomorphic to O(4)+O(5), matching the packet orientation. This route does not use FND-0154. FND-0163 records it only inside a NOT ASSERTED clause, so a proof that invokes it must cite the theorem independently. (3) This existence hinge is inherited by every argument that realises an etale chart of Hbar^bal over M_{0,18} or Conf_18. It does not by itself control Gr^W_16 H_c^{16} of the evaluation-failure model Z, nor the campaign target RED-0001.
- `FND-0176` [corroborated; {'bases': 'reduced separated finite-type C-schemes B carrying the constant type-(i) family; the C^8 witness lies inside the reduced locally Noetherian quantification of ATT-0112 clause (E)', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'counterexample': 'B=C^8 for C the affine Kummer curve of FND-0170; U isomorphic to C^8 times U_0 of dimension 10; surviving Hodge type (10,6) in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) and in the S_6-invariants of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q)', 'excluded': ['RED-0001', 'the global kernel K (FND-0168)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'transport of the j=8 first FND-0167 summand on a pure-dimension-15 atlas (FND-0171)'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['Q-coefficients over C', '(C_0,gamma_0) a geometric type-(i) fibre of H^bal, e.g. a simply-branched balanced fibre (FND-0172)', 'B reduced, separated, and of finite type over C', 'constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures', 'finite-etale S_6-transfer over Q'], 'objects': ['U isomorphic to B times U_0', 'Z=Ord(U)', 'Gr^W_m H_c^m(B;Q)(-2)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q)', 'T_16(Z)'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a geometric type-(i) fibre of H^bal in the sense of FND-0153, for instance any simply-branched balanced fibre (existence: FND-0172). Let B be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme. The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over B with fibre (C_0,gamma_0) is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base, because its classifying image is a single type-(i) point. For this family, A=P_B(pi_*L) is isomorphic to B times |L_0| isomorphic to B times P^2, the reduced-support open U_0 of |L_0| is a nonempty smooth connected affine surface (the complement of the discriminant curve of the spanned g^2_6), U is isomorphic to B times U_0, and Z=Ord(U) isomorphic to B times Z_0 is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. Poincare duality on the smooth connected surface U_0, equivalently compact-support localization of U_0 subset P^2 against the discriminant curve Delta_0 of dimension 1, yields H_c^4(U_0;Q) isomorphic to Q(-2), pure of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures for products of separated finite-type C-schemes (the compact-support form of Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Proposition 8.2.10) therefore realises H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) for every integer m, and, Q(-2) being pure of weight 4 with Gr^W exact, realises Gr^W_m H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct summand of Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q). Finite-etale transfer over Q identifies Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) with the S_6-invariants inside Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(Z;Q). Consequently any theorem asserting that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8) for every allowed clause-(E) base forces Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q) to be a finite direct sum of Q(-6) for every reduced separated finite-type C-scheme B. This last assertion is false: if C is the affine Kummer curve of FND-0170 (the smooth projective model of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x), then for B=C^8 compact-support Kunneth supplies a nonzero Hodge component of type (8,4) in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q), namely Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{tensor 4} with the type-(1,0) line of H^1(Cbar) in each of the four H_c^1 factors, and tensoring with Q(-2) produces a nonzero type-(10,6) class in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) and hence in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). Type (10,6) satisfies Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) for dim U=10 and is not of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z) is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). The exact C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem of campaign revision 4, universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, is therefore false. A repaired C66-TATE-SUPPORT must either name a specific base or atlas, or retain the FND-0167 hypotheses (H-S) including the j=6 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q). The exhibited class is the third FND-0167 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), realised as a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself on a product family, not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S); FND-0171, which blocks transport of the j=8 first summand through the corner injection on a pure-dimension-15 atlas, does not apply. Not asserted: any computation of the global kernel K, any conclusion about a fixed 15-dimensional atlas of Hbar^bal, or any statement about RED-0001.
- `FND-0177` [corroborated; {'H_S_index_disambiguation': 'fibre degree 2j for j=0,1,2 versus (H-S) j=8 for the first summand', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['transport of non-Tateness by the FND-0167 injection itself', 'compact-support Leray with nonconstant coefficients on non-product families (FND-0164)', 'RED-0001', 'T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal', 'S_6-isotypics other than S_6-invariants of the product model'], 'fibre_degrees': [0, 1, 2], 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['S reduced separated finite-type over C', 'Delta_0 closed in P^2 of dimension at most 1', 'constant or product (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family so A is the trivial P^2-bundle', 'Q-coefficients and mixed Hodge structures'], 'objects': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q)', 'Gr^W_14 H_c^{14}(S;Q)(-1)', 'Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2)', 'product families U=S x U_0 with U_0=P^2 minus Delta_0']}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme, let Delta_0 subset P^2 be a closed subscheme of dimension at most 1, and set U_0=P^2 minus Delta_0. For a product (equivalently, constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL)) family with U isomorphic to S times U_0, compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures and the projective-bundle formula identify Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S times P^2;Q) with the direct sum of three pure weight-16 summands Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^{14}(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2), corresponding to fibre degrees 2j for j=0,1,2. Compact-support localization along U_0 subset P^2 is a long exact sequence of mixed Hodge structures; at the weight-equals-degree corner Gr^W is exact, so the fibre-degree-2j projective-bundle summand of A=S times P^2 lies in the image of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) if and only if the restriction Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(P^2;Q) -> Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) vanishes. Vanishing of H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) is sufficient for that restriction to vanish, and holds whenever 2j>2 dim Delta_0. Thus the fibre-degree-2 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) always survives in such product families as a direct Kunneth summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), equivalently H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2), because H_c^4 of a curve vanishes; this is the class used by ATT-0119. If Delta_0 is nonempty and proper then H_c^0(U_0;Q)=0, so the fibre-degree-0 summand Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) does not appear in H_c^{16}(U;Q); the restriction H_c^2(P^2)->H_c^2(Delta_0) is typically nonzero for a positive-degree plane curve, so the fibre-degree-1 projective-bundle summand need not arise from U. Independently, on a non-product FND-0167 family with S of pure dimension 15, the discriminant Delta subset A has dimension 16, so Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0. This is why FND-0171 blocks transporting the (H-S) j=8 / fibre-degree-0 first summand of ATT-0118 to U, while it does not block the ATT-0119 fibre-fundamental-class class, which is already a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself. The FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into the three summands and cannot by itself transport non-Tateness from any ambient summand to U; survival of the third summand in product families is a kernel/Kunneth statement, not a reverse of that injection. Fibrewise restriction on Delta_0 does not by itself control non-product families at fibre degrees j=0,1 without a compact-support Leray argument, which FND-0164 withholds for nonconstant coefficients. No assertion is made about RED-0001, about T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal, or about S_6-isotypics other than the S_6-invariants of the product model.
- `FND-0178` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['failure of RED-0001', 'failure of T_16 on a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal', 'failure of the FND-0167 implication under (H-S) or (H-C)', 'any closed embedding, Gysin map, image, or support-exhaustion statement in M_{6,6}'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'surviving_class': 'nonzero Hodge type (10,6) in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), S_6-invariant, from the Kunneth summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S) tensor H_c^4(U_0)=Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2)', 'theorem_disproved': 'TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis', 'witness_base': 'S=C_aff^8, C_aff the affine Kummer curve of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x, equipped with the constant simply-branched balanced type-(i) family', 'witness_dimensions': {'S': 8, 'U': 10, 'Z': 10}}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let C_aff be the smooth connected affine curve obtained from the smooth projective model Cbar of y^3=x(x-1) by deleting the three ramification points of the degree-three x-map: Cbar has genus one by Riemann-Hurwitz, H_c^2(C_aff;Q)=Q(-1) of type (1,1), and Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q) is isomorphic to H^1(Cbar;Q) of types (1,0) and (0,1). Let S=C_aff^8, a smooth connected affine C-scheme of dimension 8, in particular reduced, locally Noetherian, separated, and of finite type. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places a nonzero Hodge type-(8,4) class in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q), arising from the summand Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q))^{tensor 4}. Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a simply-branched balanced type-(i) geometric fibre of H^bal (existence by FND-0172, equivalently Bujokas-Patel: the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of a general cover in H_{d,g} is balanced for g>=(d-3)(d-1), hence at (d,g)=(4,6)). The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over S with this fibre is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base: its classifying image is a single type-(i) point, hence not contained in the type-(ii) locus. For this family, U isomorphic to S times U_0 and Z isomorphic to S times Z_0, where U_0 is the reduced-support open in |L_0| isomorphic to P^2, a smooth connected surface, so H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2) of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth therefore realises Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), carrying a nonzero Hodge type-(10,6) class (permitted by Deligne's Hodge-number bound on the 10-fold U). Finite-etale transfer over Q injects this S_6-invariant class into Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). A finite direct sum of Q(-8) is pure of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z):=W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(Z;Q), dual with no extra Tate twist, is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). Consequently the exact TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem, as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus and with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis, is false. The witness lies entirely in the simply-branched locus and already in the S_6-invariant ([6]) isotypic component. The class is a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself, namely the third FND-0167 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S), so FND-0171 does not block it. This does not resolve RED-0001, does not address T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal, and does not refute the conditional implication of FND-0167, because the witness base violates (H-S) at j=6 and at j=7 (while the j=8 instance of (H-S) holds for this particular S).
- `FND-0180` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimension': 21, 'does_not_assert': ['Tate type of T or T_Z', 'support-exhaustion T_Z=T', 'closed embedding of Z', 'regular immersion, lci, or pure-codimension Gysin for Y', 'a map from the cohomology of Z to T'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'objects': ['M_{6,6}', 'H^bal', 'ordered reduced-support CE model Z', 'classifying morphism f:Z->M_{6,6}', 'Y reduced Zariski closure of the classifying image', 'U_Y=M_{6,6} minus Y', 'T=W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', 'T_Z'], 'open_bm_degree': 16, 'open_bm_weight': -16, 'ordinary_cohomology_degree': 26, 'poincare_twist': 21, 'subproblem_id': 'C66-SUPPORT-INTERFACE'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let X denote the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack M_{6,6} of dimension 21, and let T := W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(X;Q), identified by FND-0001 with W_{26} H^{26}(X;Q)(21). Let Z be the ordered reduced-support Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure scheme over a smooth finite-type scheme atlas of the balanced tetragonal stack H^bal, as supplied by the dual-confirmed ATT-0112 clause (E). The tautological smooth genus-six curve with six pairwise-disjoint sections on Z is an object of X(Z), so the universal property of X supplies a morphism f: Z -> X of locally finite-type Deligne-Mumford stacks; no monomorphism, unramifiedness, or closed-immersion claim is used. Let Y be the unique reduced closed substack of X whose underlying space is the Zariski closure of the geometric image of f; Y is independent of the choice of smooth finite-type atlas of H^bal. The source Z has dimension 20 (atlas dimension 18 plus relative dimension two of the reduced-support open of the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle), so the image of f has dimension at most 20 and Y is a proper closed substack of X; the complement U_Y := X minus Y is a nonempty dense smooth open of dimension 21. Restriction r: H^{26}(X;Q) -> H^{26}(U_Y;Q) is a morphism of mixed Hodge structures. Both groups have weights at least 26, morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for the weight filtration, and W_{26} equals Gr^W_{26} on each. Define T_Z := ker(T -> W_{26} H^{26}(U_Y;Q)(21)). Then T_Z is a pure polarizable weight -16 subobject of T, equal to the image of the degree-26 cohomology-with-supports map W_{26} H^{26}_Y(X;Q)(21) -> T, and not in general isomorphic to the supports group W_{26} H^{26}_Y(X;Q)(21) itself (the FND-0168(3a)-versus-(3b) distinction). Poincare-Verdier duality on the smooth ambient X identifies cohomology with supports along Y with Borel-Moore homology of Y and intertwines ordinary open restriction with Borel-Moore corestriction on the smooth pair (X, U_Y); consequently T_Z coincides with the image of W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> T in the sense of FND-0168(3a). This naming uses only the closed-open pair (Y, U_Y) inside the smooth stack X. It does not require a closed embedding of Z, a regular immersion or lci hypothesis on Y, purity of any codimension, or a Gysin shift by twice a codimension. Coverage is one-sided: every class in T supported on a closed subset of X contained in Y, in particular every class supported on the image of Z or on its closure, lies in T_Z; extra components of Y are not excluded. The construction asserts neither T_Z = T, nor any Tate type of T or T_Z, nor a map from the cohomology of Z. Therefore FND-0052 and FND-0168(5a)/(5b) are not obstructions to forming this C66-SUPPORT-INTERFACE datum; they remain binding wherever T_Z must be computed or shown Tate.
- `FND-0181` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q for the kernel-form localization consequence only', 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'mathematical_scope': 'Properness of the reduced classifying-image closure Y inside the smooth 21-dimensional stack M_{6,6}; upper bound dim Y<=20 coming from the H^bal-level model of dimension 18+2, not a computation of dim Y.', 'not_covered': ['equality dim Y=17 or dim Y=20', 'closed embedding of Z or of Y in M_{6,6}', 'regular immersion, lci structure, or Gysin map', 'cohomological support-exhaustion T_Z=T', 'Tate type of T or of T_Z', 'unbalanced Casnati-Ekedahl strata'], 'objects': ['H^bal', 'stack-level ordered reduced-support CE model Z', 'classifying morphism f:Z->M_{6,6}', 'Y=reduced Zariski closure of the classifying image', 'U_Y=M_{6,6} minus Y', 'kernel-form term T_Z']}]: Work over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let H=H_{4,6}(P^1) be the Deligne-Mumford stack of finite degree-four covers of a fixed P^1 by smooth connected genus-six curves, and let H^bal be the open locus where the Casnati-Ekedahl relations bundle is isomorphic to O(4)+O(5). Then H^bal is smooth of pure dimension 18 (FND-0159, FND-0162, FND-0163). Let Z be the stack-level ordered reduced-support Casnati-Ekedahl model over H^bal: the finite etale S_6-torsor of orderings of the reduced-support open U of the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle P(pi_*L). That bundle is smooth of relative dimension two, U is nonempty and dense in every fibre (FND-0134), and the ordering torsor is finite etale, so Z is smooth of pure dimension 18+2=20. Let f:Z->M_{6,6} be the classifying morphism of the tautological six-pointed smooth genus-six curve constructed in ATT-0120/CLM-0120-1, and let Y be the reduced closed substack of M_{6,6} whose underlying space is the Zariski closure of the geometric image of f (equivalently, of any smooth finite-type scheme atlas of Z; atlas independence as in CLM-0120-2). Then f is locally of finite type and quasi-DM, hence dim Y<=dim Z=20. Independently, M_{6,6} is a smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension 3*6-3+6=21. Therefore dim Y<=20<21, Y is a proper closed substack, and U_Y:=M_{6,6} minus Y is a nonempty dense open. In particular the kernel-form CE support term T_Z:=ker(T->W_{26}H^{26}(U_Y;Q)(21)) of ATT-0120 is not forced to equal T by emptiness of the complement: the geometric degeneration Y=M_{6,6} does not occur. This does not assert the cohomological support-exhaustion T_Z=T, nor that restriction to U_Y is nonzero on T; those remain separate inputs as in FND-0168(3a). The bound dim Y<=20 is not asserted to be sharp: the classifying image is PGL_2-invariant, Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] has dimension 15, and the corresponding model has dimension 17. No closed embedding of Z, regular immersion, Gysin map, or Tate type is asserted.
- `FND-0182` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'ground_field': 'C', 'not_asserted': ['support-exhaustion T_Z=T for any Y', 'Tate type of any kernel-form term', "that Y proper subset Y' implies a strict kernel enlargement", 'that extra support is non-Tate', 'any non-kernel-form construction of a subobject of T'], 'objects': ['T=W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', "closed substacks Ysubseteq Y' of M_{6,6} containing the CE classifying image", 'kernel-form terms ker(T->W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q))']}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let T := W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6}; Q), identified by Poincare duality with W_{26} H^{26}(M_{6,6}; Q)(21) (FND-0001). Let Im subset |M_{6,6}| be the set-theoretic image of the classifying morphism to M_{6,6} of the ordered reduced-support Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model of ATT-0112 clause (E). Let Y subseteq Y' be closed substacks of M_{6,6} with Im subset |Y|. Write U := M_{6,6} minus Y and U' := M_{6,6} minus Y', so U' subseteq U are smooth open substacks of dimension 21. Restriction H^{26}(M_{6,6}; Q) -> H^{26}(U'; Q) factors through H^{26}(U; Q) as a morphism of mixed Hodge structures. Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strictly compatible with the weight filtration, so W_{26} is an exact functor. Poincare duality on the smooth opens identifies W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(U; Q) with W_{26} H^{26}(U; Q)(21) and likewise for U'. Therefore ker(T -> W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(U; Q)) is contained in ker(T -> W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(U'; Q)), equivalently ker(T -> W_{26} H^{26}(U; Q)(21)) is contained in ker(T -> W_{26} H^{26}(U'; Q)(21)). A closed subset of |M_{6,6}| carries a unique reduced closed substack structure, so the reduced closed substack Y_0 whose underlying space is the Zariski closure of Im is the unique smallest closed substack containing Im, and the associated kernel T_{Z,Y_0} is the unique smallest kernel-form term among those indexed by closed substacks of M_{6,6} containing Im. This comparison is internal to that kernel-form family and does not constrain other constructions of subobjects of T. Two consequences: (i) the obligation that no class in T supported on a closed subset contained in the image of Z, or in its closure, be omitted is one-sided (the kernel may contain classes supported on extra components of Y, including points of the Zariski closure of Im that do not lie in Im) and is already met by every such Y, in particular by Y_0; (ii) a strictly larger kernel-form term cannot be obtained from a closed support contained in Y_0, so enlarging the kernel-form term toward exhaustion T_{Z,Y}=T requires a closed support not contained in Y_0 and therefore not equal to the reduced CE classifying-image closure. That extra support is not identified with the CE geometry by the kernel-form interface and is not shown Tate by that construction; showing any enlarged term Tate remains a separate C66-TATE-SUPPORT obligation. Support-exhaustion T_{Z,Y}=T is not asserted for any Y, and vanishing of restriction from T to a nonempty complement is not asserted.
- `FND-0184` [corroborated; {'campaign_objects': ['H^bal', 'M_{6,6}', 'PGL_2', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'ATT-0112/CLM-0112-7', 'ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8'], 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': None, 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero, or C', 'hypotheses': ['H and X are algebraic stacks', 'atlases are smooth and surjective of finite type, with source an algebraic space (or a scheme)', 'the classifying morphism is functorial in the 2-Yoneda sense, so tautological families pull back along morphisms of atlases', 'a morphism [H/G]->X, or equality of geometric images from H and from [H/G], requires a separate G-equivariance/G-invariance hypothesis'], 'not_covered': ['transfer of the ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8 scheme-level P^2-bundle/ordering-torsor model from atlases of H^bal to etale atlases of [H^bal/PGL_2]', 'atlas-independence of compactly supported cohomology of the atlas', 'constructibility of S (Chevalley), which is used in CLM-0120-2 but is not required for independence of the reduced closure', 'Tate type, Gysin maps, closed embeddings of Z, or support-exhaustion'], 'objects': ['algebraic stacks H and X', 'smooth surjective finite-type atlases from algebraic spaces', "2-fibre product W=V x_H V'", 'classifying morphisms f_V:Z_V->X', 'geometric image S in |X|', 'reduced closed substack Y', 'quotient presentation [H/G]']}]: Let H and X be algebraic stacks. Suppose a subset S of the geometric points |X| is defined as the image of a classifying morphism attached functorially, in the 2-Yoneda sense, to smooth surjective finite-type atlases of H: for every such atlas V->H from an algebraic space there is a finite-type morphism f_V:Z_V->X, and these morphisms are compatible with pullback along morphisms of atlases. Then for any two such atlases V->H and V'->H, the 2-fibre product W=V x_H V' exists as an algebraic space (Stacks Project Tag 04T2); the projections W->V and W->V' are smooth and surjective, hence surjective on geometric points (Tags 04XH, 04XI); and W->H is again a smooth surjective atlas. If Z_(-) is constructed only for scheme bases, one must pass to a scheme presentation of W. The tautological family on Z_W is then the pullback of the families on Z_V and Z_{V'}, so the geometric images of f_V, f_{V'}, and f_W in |X| coincide. Consequently S is independent of the atlas, and the unique reduced closed substack Y of X with |Y| equal to the Zariski closure of S (Tag 0509) is independent of the atlas. Common refinement of atlases of H does not by itself produce a morphism [H/G]->X or identify S with the image arising from an atlas of the quotient: a morphism [H/G]->X exists if and only if the classifying morphism from H is G-equivariant, equivalently the X-valued moduli point is G-invariant on geometric points (Tag 04WM). This lemma does not assert that a scheme-level tautological model constructed on atlases of H transfers to etale atlases of [H/G], and it does not assert atlas-independence of compactly supported cohomology of the atlas. In the campaign case (g,n)=(6,6), with H=H^bal the balanced tetragonal stack, X=M_{6,6}, and G=PGL_2, the extra invariance is ATT-0112/CLM-0112-7; the failure of ATT-0112/CLM-0112-8 to transfer to atlases of Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] is the separate finding FND-0187.","numLines":12,"startLine":126,"totalLines":193}}}
